 "about": "Sealed order and marker records (docs/protocol/order-records.md). Texts are the canonical plaintext (UTF-8); a row key has a real line feed. \"limits\" cases are built by the rule below, in canonical bytes: d is one tag of 31 zeros and a 1; h is h0, h1, h2 (as many as the rows use); a session id is 00000000-0000-4000-8000- and the number as 12 digits; row i has host i % 3, that session, register [i + 1, 0, k and i in base 36 as 3 characters, 1 if i % 20 is 0 else 0]; membership j (for j below its count) is for row 4j and names group j % groups, register [300 + j, 0, the group id]; group n has id 00000000-0000-4000-8000- and n as 12 digits, name Group n, register [900 + n, 0, name]; tombstone t is host 0, session 00000000-0000-4000-9000- and t as 12 digits, [2000 + t, 0, 20400].",
